    "sentence_translations": [
      "Crow's Beak",
      "",
      "Saturday afternoon, Little Ming’s family drove to the lake to barbecue.",
      "Before leaving, Little Ming said: “There are so many clouds. Will it rain later?”",
      "Little Ming's mother said: “Of course not. The weather forecast said it will just be cloudy.”",
      "",
      "An hour later, they arrived at the lake.",
      "When they took out the grill and the food, it began to rain.",
      "They therefore decided to drive back to the city and eat barbecue at a restaurant.",
      "Little Ming said: “The rain is so heavy. There might be a traffic jam on the way back.”",
      "Halfway back, they were really caught in a traffic jam and had to drive slowly.",
      "",
      "Two hours later, they finally got into the city.",
      "Little Ming said: “We need to be quick.  The restaurant might ... ”",
      "Little Ming’s mother quickly said: “Stop! You are really a ‘crow's beak’.”",
      "“All bad things that you’ve said happened today. Don’t speak any more from now on.”"
    ]
  }
